Changes PitchGuide needs on top of the official JUCE 8.0.14 release
(third_party/JUCE). CMake applies this patch to the submodule when it
configures the project; see "JUCE patches" in CMakeLists.txt.

They are the six commits of the Session Loops JUCE fork
(https://github.com/SessionLoops/JUCE, by Jie Chen), which PitchNet was
built against, squashed into one patch:

  02042b7d allow undo and redo shortcuts
  468e6afc support for ARA AAX
  8c071ce9 revert function name to isTimeStretchReflectingTempo()
  d9c9776d Update juce_audio_plugin_client_VST3.cpp
  c39890a3 Update juce_audio_plugin_client_AAX.cpp
  2b4ea930 fix au capture failed bug

What they do:
  - VST3: forward Ctrl/Cmd shortcuts (undo, redo, Match Reference...) that
    hosts such as FL Studio would otherwise keep from the plug-in editor.
  - AudioProcessorListener::ChangeDetails::withTailLengthChanged(), and the
    AU wrapper reporting a changed tail length to the host.
  - ARA in the AAX wrapper.

Like JUCE, these changes are available under the GNU AGPLv3. The patch
reproduces the fork's files exactly; the files use CRLF line endings, as
they do in JUCE, so this file must not be converted (see .gitattributes).

